    "title": "Santa Rosa County 4-H hosting bluebird house building workshop for kids - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Summer Poole ,\n1 hours ago\nSANTA ROSA COUNTY, Fla. ( WKRG ) — Interested in learning how to build a birdhouse? Well, the Santa Rosa County 4-H is offering you the opportunity to learn.\nTeens allegedly assault woman at Mobile hospital The Bluebird Box Building Workshop will be held on Saturday, Oct. 11, from 10 a.m. to 2 p.m., according to a news release.\nThe cost to take part in the event, which is being held at the Santa Rosa County Extension Office, is $15 and is open to kids ages 8 to 18.\nThe workshop will teach kids the need for the local bluebird population, how bluebirds benefit the community and how they can help bluebirds at home, according to the release.\nGulf Shores tennis center receives national award Registration is open until Thursday, Oct. 8.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WKRG News 5.\n1",
